<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rĕmus</span></b> , i, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the brother of
				Romulus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 2,
				2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Div. 2, 38, 80</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2,
				533</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3, 41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 56</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">5, 464</span></i>.—In the poets, as the ancestor of
			the Romans, instead of the more usual Romulus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glubit magnanimos Remi nepotes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					58, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 73</span></i>
			 Rupert.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 76, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regna prima Remi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					2, 1, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 1, 9: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culmina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 2, 7, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 6, 80.</div>
